    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "we checked the ink density and the temp probes seem fine, but the transfer is still inconsistent. sometimes it's okay, but then a whole batch comes out looking like the color just disappeared or didn't take at all. is there a specific timing or pressure threshold we might be missing that causes it to just fail like that?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Inconsistent transfers can be caused by pressure fluctuations, heat press dwell time, and temperature variations. Try adjusting the pressure to 10-15 psi higher than recommended, as this can help ensure even heat distribution and transferred ink. Dwell time is also crucial, ensuring the heat press doesn't cool down too quickly before printing. A longer dwell time of 30-60 seconds can help improve transfer uniformity.",
